3. RISK OF DATA LOSS AND SYSTEM CHANGES — READ CAREFULLY

Alter modifies application packages and writes files to device storage. These
operations are inherently risky. In particular:
- patching, injecting, re-signing, repackaging, and merging APKs produce
  modified files that may be incomplete, corrupted, or non-functional, and that
  may fail to install or may crash on launch;
- an operation can be interrupted, run out of storage, or fail partway and
  leave files in an inconsistent state;
- installing a modified or re-signed app over an existing one can replace or
  delete that app's data; a signature change can require a full uninstall and
  wipe its data;
- dumping and extraction write potentially large files to shared or
  app-specific storage and may overwrite files that already carry the same
  name;
- some features require broad storage permissions (including "All files
  access") to move results into an open folder.

YOU USE THESE FEATURES AT YOUR OWN RISK. Always keep a separate backup of any
app, file, or data that matters to you before processing it with Alter. The
App is not responsible for lost, corrupted, or overwritten files, for apps that
stop working, or for any consequence that a modified package causes on your
device or account (including, for example, bans imposed by a service on
modified clients).


